  "from": "2024-06",
  "confidence": "low",
  "drawnOn": "B38M",
  "description": "Arajet's tenth 737 MAX 8, HI1101 'Los Haitises', delivered in June 2024: the standard white scheme with the parrot fin, violet cowlings and winglets, and a long ribbon in the Dominican flag's colors waving the length of the fuselage. The ribbon is a red band over a blue band with white between. It starts under the cockpit as blue over red, crosses over in a white diagonal (the flag's cross) by the forward door, then runs red over blue up over the forward windows, drops in a twisting loop to the belly, climbs to the crown ahead of the wing, dips behind the wing, climbs again over the windows behind it, loops down once more and rises to end at the crown ahead of the tailplane. A smaller 'arajet' over the forward windows clear of it; the flag and registration over the aft windows.",
  "sources": [
    {
      "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Boeing_737_Max_-_HI1101_-_Arajet.jpg",
