  "notes": "Drawn from one photo of the left side (HI1101, 2024-06-10), so low: each band was read as a centerline with its width (about 15 px of a 1600 px photo, 0.35 m) and turned into areas on the fitted shape, not traced edge by edge. Where the ribbon passes behind the engine and wing (about x 0.47-0.55) its path is joined up by guess. The ends of the bands at the white cross are drawn square; on the aircraft they're cut on the cross's diagonal. The twists in the loops are drawn as the bands overlapping. The right side isn't in an open photo: drawn the same way round, which may be wrong. Not drawn: the registration, 'Los Haitises' under the cockpit.",
  "history": "New 2026-11-26. Delivered in June 2024 (Arajet's tenth 737 MAX 8). Still flying in it in 2025 by spotter listings (not cited)."
